#: src/i18n/harvested.ts
msgid "Step five of the wizard lists exactly what this call asks for. Every funder sets their own list, so read the one on your grant rather than assuming.\n"
"\n"
"A typical list is: a detailed budget covering the full amount requested, proof of registration, recent financial statements, a workplan, and any letters of support. Required items are marked; the rest strengthen the application without being mandatory.\n"
"\n"
"Accepted formats are PDF, Word, Excel, CSV, Markdown, plain text and images, up to 25MB per file. If a file is refused, the reason appears under the file picker — it is either the size or the format, nothing else.\n"
"\n"
"Name each file for what it is. An assessor reading twenty applications should be able to tell your budget from your workplan without opening either.\n"
"\n"
"These files are private. They are attached to your application, visible only to you and the people assessing the grant, and never listed on the public grant page. The Documents panel on the grant page itself is the funder's — it holds the call and its annexes, not your submission."
msgstr "El paso cinco del asistente indica exactamente lo que solicita esta convocatoria. Cada financiador define su propia lista, así que consulte la de su subvención en lugar de dar nada por supuesto.\n"
""

